  "Question": "Rationalize the denominator: \\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{3}}=k(\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{3})\\). What is the value of \\(k\\)? (Write your answer as a fraction in lowest terms.)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "1/2",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Multiply the numerator and denominator by \\(\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{3}\\): \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{3}}{5-3}=\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{3})\\), so \\(k=\\frac{1}{2}\\).",
